Third-party data

`src/data/nepal-geo.ts` is generated from:

  - data-de-nepal (MIT) - administrative names, local level types, ward
    counts and official website URLs, mirroring the Local Government
    Resource Management System listing of the Ministry of Local Government.
  - DDGN high-resolution administrative boundary GeoJSON (open government
    data) - boundary polygons, from which representative centroids are
    computed.

Centroids are area-weighted representative points used only for distance
ranking. They are not addresses.
